Track 2: The Compass Swallows Salt
- Story & Context: Camp cartographer Silas spent three weeks tracking the shifting alkali borders of Soda Lake while nursing a fried vacuum tube and a broken heart. He confessed over late-night cider that he had deliberately recalibrated the caravan's navigation beacons to steer their sound system straight past his ex-lover's remote homestead, all to flaunt the euphoric new rhythms they were carving out in the salt dunes. With bitter dust crunching between his teeth and his fingers blistering against chrome guitar strings, he howled out across the dry pan: "I drew the border crooked just to hear your floorboards shake!"
